{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"9837d5c74f2314365fabb37f881e2bdceaeef0ef"},"timestamp":1466844156,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNjIyNzEyMzE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/588","origin":"github"},"title":"File hierarchy for defined subset","message":"It wold be cool if one had the option to copy only the directory structure leading up to the branch for which one needs to install the data:\n\ne.g from this structure, of which one only needs the subdirectory `files`:\n\nsci-biology/\n├── abacas\n│   ├── abacas-1.3.1.ebuild\n│   ├── Manifest\n│   └── metadata.xml\n├── act-bin\n│   ├── act-bin-13.0.0.ebuild\n│   ├── Manifest\n│   └── metadata.xml\n├── afni\n│   ├── afni-0_pre20130927.ebuild\n│   ├── afni-0_pre20141212.ebuild\n│   ├── afni-9999.ebuild\n│   ├── ChangeLog\n│   ├── Manifest\n│   └── metadata.xml\n...\n├── fsa\n│   ├── fsa-1.15.7.ebuild\n│   ├── Manifest\n│   └── metadata.xml\n├── fsl\n│   ├── files\n│   │   ├── 99fsl\n│   │   ├── fsl-5.0.4-headers.patch\n│   │   ├── fsl-5.0.4-setup.patch\n│   │   ├── fsl-5.0.6-fsldir_redux.patch\n│   │   ├── fsl-5.0.8-fsldir_redux.patch\n│   │   ├── fsl-5.0.8-headers.patch\n│   │   └── fsl-5.0.8-setup.patch\n│   ├── fsl-5.0.8.ebuild\n│   ├── Manifest\n│   └── metadata.xml \n...\n\nyou would only get the following paths:\n\n**sci-biology**/\n├── abacas\n│   ├── abacas-1.3.1.ebuild\n│   ├── Manifest\n│   └── metadata.xml\n├── act-bin\n│   ├── act-bin-13.0.0.ebuild\n│   ├── Manifest\n│   └── metadata.xml\n├── afni\n│   ├── afni-0_pre20130927.ebuild\n│   ├── afni-0_pre20141212.ebuild\n│   ├── afni-9999.ebuild\n│   ├── ChangeLog\n│   ├── Manifest\n│   └── metadata.xml\n...\n├── fsa\n│   ├── fsa-1.15.7.ebuild\n│   ├── Manifest\n│   └── metadata.xml\n├── **fsl**\n│   ├── **files**\n│   │   ├── 99fsl\n│   │   ├── fsl-5.0.4-headers.patch\n│   │   ├── fsl-5.0.4-setup.patch\n│   │   ├── fsl-5.0.6-fsldir_redux.patch\n│   │   ├── fsl-5.0.8-fsldir_redux.patch\n│   │   ├── fsl-5.0.8-headers.patch\n│   │   └── fsl-5.0.8-setup.patch\n│   ├── fsl-5.0.8.ebuild\n│   ├── Manifest\n│   └── metadata.xml \n...\n\nthis can already be done wth two commands:\n\n`datalad install http://myhost/sci-biology ; datalad install sci-biology/fsl/files`\n\nBut this seems a common enough use case, to warrant an own command :-/ for me in fact it would be the main use case.\nIt is important I think to keep the directory structure when installing a submodue so that people can rely on the same path structures.","files":null}]}